<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cleobulus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cleobulus was a tyrant of Lindos on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> in the 6th century BCE, counted among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-sages-of-greece">Seven Sages of Greece</a>. Ancient tradition credits him with rebuilding the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> Lindia on the acropolis of Lindos and with sayings such as 'Moderation is best'. His daughter Cleobulina was known as a composer of riddles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cleobulus.jpg" alt="Cleobulus" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cleovoulos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
